WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.780
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.292
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:16.018
Unit thirteen: Saving Water. In this unit, you will give advice about saving water.

4
00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:17.844
Water.

5
00:00:18.544 --> 00:00:21.681
Water means the clear liquid we drink and wash with.

6
00:00:21.981 --> 00:00:23.818
Water is important for life.

7
00:00:24.518 --> 00:00:27.426
Your turn. Say: Water.

8
00:00:30.126 --> 00:00:30.918
Water.

9
00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:32.581
Tap.

10
00:00:33.281 --> 00:00:35.443
Tap means the thing you turn to get water.

11
00:00:35.743 --> 00:00:36.918
Turn off the tap.

12
00:00:37.618 --> 00:00:39.841
Your turn. Say: Tap.

13
00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:43.264
Tap.

14
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.147
Turn off.

15
00:00:45.847 --> 00:00:49.576
Turn off means to stop water, light or a machine.

16
00:00:49.876 --> 00:00:52.131
Turn off the tap when you brush your teeth.

17
00:00:52.831 --> 00:00:55.890
Your turn. Say: Turn off.

18
00:00:58.590 --> 00:00:59.324
Turn off.

19
00:01:00.317 --> 00:01:01.051
Shower.

20
00:01:01.751 --> 00:01:05.039
Shower means a way to wash your body under running water.

21
00:01:05.339 --> 00:01:06.897
I take a short shower.

22
00:01:07.597 --> 00:01:10.714
Your turn. Say: Shower.

23
00:01:13.414 --> 00:01:14.334
Shower.

24
00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:16.223
Save.

25
00:01:16.923 --> 00:01:19.817
Save means to keep something and not waste it.

26
00:01:20.117 --> 00:01:21.594
We should save water.

27
00:01:22.294 --> 00:01:25.167
Your turn. Say: Save.

28
00:01:27.867 --> 00:01:28.613
Save.

29
00:01:29.617 --> 00:01:30.444
Waste.

30
00:01:31.144 --> 00:01:33.352
Waste means to use more than you need.

31
00:01:33.652 --> 00:01:34.967
Don't waste water.

32
00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:38.133
Your turn. Say: Waste.

33
00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:41.649
Waste.

34
00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:43.384
Bucket.

35
00:01:44.084 --> 00:01:47.036
Bucket means an open container for carrying water.

36
00:01:47.336 --> 00:01:48.871
Fill the bucket with water.

37
00:01:49.571 --> 00:01:52.351
Your turn. Say: Bucket.

38
00:01:55.051 --> 00:01:55.773
Bucket.

39
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:57.668
Plants.

40
00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:01.796
Plants means living green things like trees and flowers.

41
00:02:02.096 --> 00:02:04.235
I water the plants every morning.

42
00:02:04.935 --> 00:02:07.738
Your turn. Say: Plants.

43
00:02:10.438 --> 00:02:11.300
Plants.

44
00:02:12.283 --> 00:02:14.596
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:14.896 --> 00:02:17.175
Rithy, how can we save water?

46
00:02:18.483 --> 00:02:21.214
We should turn off the tap when we brush our teeth.

47
00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:24.914
Good idea! What about showers?

48
00:02:26.217 --> 00:02:27.972
We should take short showers.

49
00:02:29.283 --> 00:02:30.818
And what shouldn't we do?

50
00:02:32.117 --> 00:02:35.582
We shouldn't waste water. We can use a bucket for the plants!

51
00:02:36.883 --> 00:02:39.707
Grammar focus: Should and shouldn't.

52
00:02:40.007 --> 00:02:43.008
You should turn off the tap. You shouldn't waste water.

53
00:02:43.308 --> 00:02:47.179
'Shouldn't' means 'should not'. Use it to say something is a bad idea.

54
00:02:48.183 --> 00:02:51.103
Now read and listen. Every Drop Counts.

55
00:02:51.403 --> 00:02:54.900
Water is important for people, animals and plants.

56
00:02:56.183 --> 00:03:00.482
In the dry season, water is hard to find, so we should save it.

57
00:03:01.783 --> 00:03:04.166
I turn off the tap when I brush my teeth.

58
00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.448
I take a short shower, not a long one.

59
00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.237
I use water from a bucket for the plants.

60
00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:16.249
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:16.549 --> 00:03:18.305
You blank waste water.

62
00:03:18.605 --> 00:03:21.817
A, shouldn't. B, should. C, shoulds.

63
00:03:25.817 --> 00:03:28.176
The answer is A: shouldn't.

64
00:03:29.683 --> 00:03:32.205
Turn blank the tap when you brush your teeth.

65
00:03:32.505 --> 00:03:35.334
A, on. B, off. C, in.

66
00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.860
The answer is B: off.

67
00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:46.534
An open container for carrying water is a blank.

68
00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:50.615
A, bucket. B, shower. C, tap.

69
00:03:54.617 --> 00:03:57.069
The answer is A: bucket.

70
00:03:58.583 --> 00:04:02.153
Now it's your turn to speak. How can you save water at home?

71
00:04:07.453 --> 00:04:11.786
I should turn off the tap when I brush my teeth, and I shouldn't play with the hose.

72
00:04:12.086 --> 00:04:13.668
Excellent answer, Rithy!

73
00:04:14.683 --> 00:04:18.891
Great work today! You learned eight new words and should and shouldn't.

74
00:04:19.191 --> 00:04:23.678
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

75
00:04:23.978 --> 00:04:26.700
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.792
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

